    "body": "## Purpose\r\ntests/compile/h100/test_startup.py requires CUDA/H100. The `intel-ci` pipeline runs this test area's commands without honoring the `device` selector, executing the file on XPU where torch's compile cache ends up disabled, so every `cold_artifacts_saved`/`warm_artifacts_saved` assertion fails with `got 0`.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\nAdd `current_platform.is_cuda()` skip, same pattern used elsewhere in tests/compile/ (e.g. test_tp2_async_tp.py).\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\nModule now collects as skipped on non-CUDA platforms; full run requires H100 hardware, exercised by existing CUDA CI.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
